[h2]Placement[/h2]
[list]
[*]A straight crossing of one to three consecutive coast or lake tiles, with usable land at both ends. Deep ocean and bent bridges are not supported.
[*]Every bridge water tile must belong to the same city that builds it. Tiles from another city cannot be included, even under the same civilization.
[*]Bridge tiles cannot contain resources or other districts. Removable features and improvements are listed before construction. Cancelling leaves them intact; confirming allows their removal during construction. Feature removal still requires the relevant technology and grants no builder harvest yields.
[*]Mountains, canals or cliffs blocking a bridgehead can make the shore unsuitable.
[/list]

[h2]Feedback[/h2]
Keep BridgeSpan enabled in saves containing its bridges. For bug reports, include a bridge screenshot and reproduction steps. A save from before the issue is especially useful.

[h2]One-click diagnostics[/h2]
For bug reports, open the diagnostics client, click “生成诊断包” (Create diagnostics package), and send the desktop ZIP plus an error screenshot to the author. It automatically collects and organizes bridge logs; no installation or automatic upload. The current client UI is in Simplified Chinese.
[url=https://github.com/civs6-mods/BridgeSpan/releases/tag/diagnostics-v1.0.0]Download BridgeSpan diagnostics for Windows[/url]

[h2]Source & Contributions[/h2]
Help improve BridgeSpan! Report bugs, suggest features, contribute translations or testing, work on Lua / UI or bridge models and art, or submit a pull request on GitHub.
[url=https://github.com/civs6-mods/BridgeSpan]GitHub source code & contributions[/url]
